    "preset": "hyperpop",
    "version": 3,
    "note": "Untuned v1 ranges. These are starting brackets, deliberately wide. Narrow them with `npm run narrow` against real ratings; do not hand-guess them. master.driveTargetDb is the loudness control: the mix is measured at its loudest section and driven to exactly that short-term RMS before the master chain, so every stage downstream has a known operating point and every seed gets the amount of gain IT needs rather than the same amount. bass.bias is deliberately near zero: asymmetric shaping on a 40 Hz sub produces DC that a blocker cannot remove without eating the fundamental, so even harmonics on the 808 come from drive and fold instead. bass.octave defaults to -1: that is the 808's register (31-55 Hz fundamental). 0 puts the fundamental at 62-110 Hz, which is a bass guitar, and is kept reachable but rare. master.satDrive is deliberately NOT widened: the saturator's makeup, 1/(1+(drive-1)*0.8), compensates the small-signal gain and is blind to what the saturation does to peaks, so above about 1.5 it removes 5 dB of peak the chain never gets back and the master stops reaching its ceiling. Widening it needs a peak-referenced makeup first.",
